{"name":"Green Fiasco","hex":"#aaee00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"fiasco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden or unexpected failure.","A ludicrous or humiliating situation. Some effort that went quite wrong."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiasco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fiasco (bottle)","blocks":[{"text":"A fiasco is a traditional Italian style of bottle, usually with a round body and bottom, partially or completely covered with a close-fitting straw basket. The basket is typically made of sala, a swamp weed, sun-dried and blanched with sulfur. The basket provides protection during transportation and handling, and also a flat base for the container. Thus the glass bottle can have a round bottom, which is much simpler to make by glassblowing. Fiaschi can be efficiently packed for transport, with the necks of inverted bottles safely tucked into the spaces between the baskets of upright ones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg/330px-Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiasco_(bottle)","wikidata":"Q23676"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF/lossy-page1-500px-Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF/lossy-page1-1280px-Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF/lossy-page1-500px-Fiasco_IMV_01282.TIF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glazed terracotta flask dating back to the New Kingdom of Egypt. Museo Egizio, Turin.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFiasco_IMV_01282.TIF"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Vin_Chianti.jpg/120px-Vin_Chianti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Vin_Chianti.jpg/250px-Vin_Chianti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&